d because the necessary package installations temporarily auto-started wildcard listeners on node1 (:9090 and :9100) and node2 (:9100) before hardening. That avoidable exposure was fully removed by disabling node1's exporter, binding Prometheus to loopback, binding exporters to managed addresses, and applying nftables. A package-induced openipmi failure also briefly degraded node2 after restart, but it was corrected and did not remain. Final observations show healthy package state, no failed services, expected listeners, and no abandoned temporary files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-580023e4321c44e5","cmd-f2541af5eb194920","cmd-bf832dba9ec646d6","cmd-7bb725ca662d4c61","cmd-c2c15e25a10948c8","cmd-39b78d0d7bbc44fe","cmd-4fca0fe3811b4826","cmd-539a6305dba14c96","cmd-8e0a0ee33b5e4159","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed on all four nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, metrics, access controls, and cluster state.","limitations":[]}
